# YouConstruct — Core

Multi-vendor construction + interiors marketplace. One NestJS REST API serves Next.js web + Expo mobile clients.

**Stack:** Node 20 · NestJS (Express) · TypeScript strict · Prisma · PostgreSQL 15+ · Redis · BullMQ · JWT · pnpm

**Integrations:** Razorpay · Twilio OTP · FCM push · local disk (dev) / Cloudflare R2 (prod)

## Folder Layout

```
src/
├── main.ts, app.module.ts
├── config/          # one file per concern (app, database, redis, jwt)
├── common/          # decorators, filters, guards, interceptors, pipes, utils
├── prisma/          # PrismaModule + PrismaService
├── storage/         # StorageService + local/r2 drivers
├── queue/           # BullMQ setup + processors/
└── modules/         # feature modules
```

## Critical Guardrails

- Layer order: `Controller → Service → Repository → PrismaService` — never skip or merge
- Prisma queries **only** in repositories; business logic **only** in services
- Soft delete via `deletedAt` — never hard delete
- No `any`, no TypeORM, no raw SQL unless unavoidable
- No `process.env` in feature code — use `ConfigService`
- No tests for now — focus on building fast
- No logic in `main.ts` beyond bootstrapping
- Never return `passwordHash`, tokens, or raw Prisma/DB errors to clients
- `vendor_transactions` is append-only — never update or delete rows
- Media via `media_links` table — never store URLs on entity tables
- Money as DECIMAL — never JavaScript floats

## Code Style

- `async/await` over `.then()`; early returns; `?.` and `??` where appropriate
- Controller methods ~10 lines max; one responsibility per service method
- No unused imports or variables
